==Rules==
{{ColosseumRule|Dirt Cheap}}

==Battleground==
*1 [[Gobble]] spawns.
*Infinite [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 40~43.33 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,300f</sup>.
*2 [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 8 seconds<sup>240f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[M. Ost]] spawns as the boss.
**2 [[Gobble]]s spawn, delay 46.67~50 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,500f</sup>.
**2 [[Li'l Bun Bun]]s spawn, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.
**3 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 70% HP:
**1 [[Pterowl Hazuku]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Angelic Beast Rajakong]] spawns.
**2 [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 70 seconds<sup>2,100f</sup>, delay 70~73.33 seconds<sup>2,100f~2,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage looks terrifying, until one realizes that it's practically impossible to run out of money. Most Uber Super Rares, Legend Rares, and Mythicals can have some use made out of them. Take [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] for pure damage, [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] as your main Meatshield, [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]] for guarding against the Relics, and [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] for the Gobbles and Pterowl Hazuku. Aside from these, literally every cat unit in the game benefits from the cost change.

